  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Basel Framework: OPE25.8 ILM formula, BIC = 0",
      "summary": "The OPE25.8 ILM formula has no rule for BIC equal to zero when a bucket 1 bank is allowed to use loss data.",
      "impact": "Position: Bucket 1 bank under discretion to use loss data, BI 0, losses 10 per year (LC 150) Reading a: Formula: LC/BIC with BIC 0 -> undefined Reading b: ILM=1 as bucket 1 rule -> ORC 0 Difference: undefined vs 0",
      "correction": "Clarify or correct the cited passage so that the rule and its references give one result for the stated case."
    }
  },
